# Start the per-user Epomaker daemon when the keyboard appears.
#
# Companion to 70-epomaker-dynatab.rules: that rule grants the active seat an
# ACL on the HID nodes (TAG+="uaccess"), this one asks the user's systemd
# instance to start epomaker-daemon.service when a matching keyboard is added.
#
# Notes:
#   * TAG+="systemd" is what makes udev hand the event to systemd at all;
#     without it SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS is ignored.
#   * Match SUBSYSTEM=="usb" for the device itself. A usb-device match would
#     fire for every interface, so the service would be started several times
#     per plug-in.
#   * SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS is queued for the user that owns the device, which
#     requires a login session on a seat (see the README's headless section).
SUBSYSTEM=="usb", ATTRS{idVendor}=="3151", ATTR{idProduct}=="4015", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_USER_WANTS}+="epomaker-daemon.service"
